3333334,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":83268.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":2485.0,"requests":6}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the load-error finding key is extracted given mapping_config emits TWO message-prefix formats ('[mapping.<where>]:' for axis/hierarchy/layer errors vs '[mapping].<where>:' for vocab errors), and add a load-error test whose message uses the '[mapping].<where>:' vocab form so the extraction is proven for both.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mapping_config._parse_hierarchy: f\"[mapping.{where}]: rank for {key!r} must be an integer...\"","mapping_config._parse_vocab: f\"[mapping].{where}: expected a list of strings...\" (dot AFTER the closing bracket)","MappingConfigError 'carries no structured attribute', so the key can only come from the message string","Plan's offline load-error test case is 'a load-time one (non-integer hierarchy)' — the format that DOES match, so the vocab-format mismatch is untested"],"finding":"The load-error finding-key extraction assumes a single '[mapping.<where>]:' message prefix, but mapping_config emits two distinct prefix formats — axis/hierarchy/layer errors use '[mapping.<where>]:' while vocabulary-declaration errors use '[mapping].<where>:' (dot after the bracket). A single-format parser would fail to name the key on a malformed statuses/issue_types/link_types vocab load error, yet the plan's only load-error test (non-integer hierarchy) uses the first format and would still pass — masking the gap.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2d376e7a02ed1461","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Offline checks: 'whose key is read from the error message's [mapping.<where>]: prefix'","norm_id":"n4544a5bde1a194ba","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator writes a malformed [mapping.default.statuses] (e.g. a non-list value); doctor emits an error finding but cannot extract/name the key from the '[mapping].statuses:' message"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Match both prefix shapes (e.g. a regex like r'\\[mapping[.\\]]([\\w.]*)' or split on the first ':' then strip the '[mapping' framing), or add a structured 'where' attribute to MappingConfigError at the raise sites so doctor need not parse the message at all.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the abandoned-thread cleanup/accumulation bound: confirm the daemon thread's Jira socket is eventually released (or bound the transport with a timeout so it cannot hang indefinitely) and note that at most one such thread exists per doctor run so it cannot accumulate in a persistent MCP-server host.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.917,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the probe call runs under an explicit doctor-side bounded wall-clock timeout — a daemon worker thread whose result(timeout=…) bound is a module constant (default 10s) … a timed-out thread is abandoned and doctor returns promptly'","ABSENCE: no statement about the abandoned thread's socket/transport cleanup or bounded accumulation when doctor runs repeatedly in a persistent host process (MCP server)"],"finding":"The live-drift check spawns a daemon worker thread bounded by `result(timeout=…)` and, on timeout, 'a timed-out thread is abandoned' — but the plan does not specify the RETIRE/cleanup path for the abandoned thread. It still holds a live Jira transport/socket; the plan does not state whether abandoned threads can accumulate across repeated doctor invocations in a long-lived host (e.g. the MCP server process) or how the underlying socket is eventually released.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fceae8fe4e18d8f8b","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Live-drift check: 'a daemon worker thread whose result(timeout=…) bound is a module constant … a timed-out thread is abandoned'","norm_id":"n68dfb0b0cee1ad56","priority":0.033,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An MCP-server host that invokes doctor repeatedly while Jira is hanging accumulates abandoned worker threads each holding an open socket until the transport's own (unset — S8 sets no client timeout) timeout fires, so resources may leak until process restart"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence noting the worker thread is daemon-scoped and its transport carries its own bounded timeout (or is closed on abandonment), so no more than one such thread exists per doctor invocation and abandoned sockets are reclaimed rather than accumulating in a long-lived host.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capab